<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  launchd's socket activation: launchd listens on the adapter socket, and starts claude-ide-server at the first connection
  (an adapter that connects, or one that starts the server itself and connects to it). Nothing runs until then. With the
  idle-timeout switch, as below, the server ends when the last adapter has been gone for that many seconds; the socket
  stays with launchd, and the next connection starts the server again. (A comment of a property list cannot have two
  hyphens in a row in it, so the switch is not spelt out here.)

  SockPathName cannot use $TMPDIR or ~, so @SOCKET@ is filled in when the file is installed, with the path that the
  adapters look for by default, and the directory is made (launchd does not make it):

    sock="$(getconf DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR)claude-ide-server-$(id -u)/adapter.sock"
    mkdir -p -m 700 "$(dirname "$sock")"
    sed "s#@SOCKET@#$sock#" contrib/launchd/dev.small-gear-lab.claude-ide-server.plist \
      > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.small-gear-lab.claude-ide-server.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.small-gear-lab.claude-ide-server.plist

  To take it out again: launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/dev.small-gear-lab.claude-ide-server

  Change the path of the executable below to where it is. The name of the socket, "adapter", is the one that the server
  asks launchd for.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>dev.small-gear-lab.claude-ide-server</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/local/bin/claude-ide-server</string>
    <string>--idle-timeout</string>
    <string>300</string>
  </array>
  <key>Sockets</key>
  <dict>
    <key>adapter</key>
    <dict>
      <key>SockPathName</key>
      <string>@SOCKET@</string>
      <!-- 0600, in decimal: the socket is the user's alone. -->
      <key>SockPathMode</key>
      <integer>384</integer>
    </dict>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
